WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.772
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.082 --> 00:00:06.630
 I'm Chris Voss.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.260
And over the next 30 days,
you will learn key negotiation

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.720
skills you can use to become
a more confident colleague,

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.710
trusted leader, and advance
your professional life.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.320
You're going to practice and use
12 proven negotiation tactics

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.650
that I developed as
an FBI negotiator.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.120
The upward inflection helps
harsh things land gently.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.320
When you mirror, it starts
to help you focus more

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.400
on the other person.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.298
If you're curious, if
you're actually curious,

00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:39.840
it's going to come
out in your voice.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.520
"How am I supposed to
continue working for you

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.000
if I'm not getting paid?"

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.390
As you progress, the tools
will build on each other.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.450
First, you will learn how
to build trust and rapport

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.320
at work.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.320
Then you will learn how to
strengthen your influence

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.120
with calibrated
questioning techniques.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.470
Finally, you will learn how
to create epiphanies in order

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.960
to get to the agreement
or to get the agreement

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.200
to come to you.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.110
During our time together, there
will be interactive practice

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.280
scenarios with the community
of other fellow negotiators.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.560
Collaboration
between colleagues,

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.910
that's really a negotiation.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.270
And when your intent
is to collaborate

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.030
with people for a
better result, then it's

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:26.060
always appropriate to negotiate.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.540
I'm Chris Voss, and
this is MasterClass.

